core_rev_volatility":80.5,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":-0.0311775672660195,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":100.0,"_gate_piotroski":8,"_gp_piotroski":true,"_score_piotroski":88.9,"_gate_spread":0.0015243690194435972,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":0.8,"_gate_roic_consistency":0.4833532746029947,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":19.4,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.011299999639234698,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":37.1,"_gate_pool_share":0.8049837336976833,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":100.0,"_gate_rev_durability":-0.028864661122878665,"_gp_rev_durability":false,"_score_rev_durability":10.6,"_gate_fcf_durability":-0.1688404443097552,"_gp_fcf_durability":false,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":0.00015485924860448864,"_gp_margins":true,"_score_margins":50.2,"_gate_fund_growth":0.07251986065443174,"_gp_fund_growth":true,"_score_fund_growth":72.5,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.13329391070529784,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":100.0,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.06096873793430646,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":100.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.0070976431729140935,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":88.2,"_gate_insider_own":0.012180001,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":8.1,"_gate_insider_buying":0.333,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":33.3,"pf":[],"description_full":"Harley-Davidson, Inc. manufactures and sells motorcycles in the United States and internationally. The company operates in three segments: Harley-Davidson Motor Company, LiveWire, and Harley-Davidson Financial Services. The Harley-Davidson Motor Company segment designs, manufactures, and sells motorcycles, including cruiser, trike, Grand American touring, standard, sportbike, adventure touring, and dual sport, as well as motorcycle parts, accessories, and apparel, as well as licenses its trademarks and related services. This segment sells its products to retail customers through a network of independent dealers, as well as e-commerce channels. The LiveWire segment sells electric motorcycles, balance bikes for kids, electric bikes, parts and accessories, apparel, and related parts and services. The Harley-Davidson Financial Services segment provides wholesale financing services, such as floorplan and open-account financing of motorcycles, and parts and accessories; and retail financing services, such as installment lending for the purchase of new and used Harley-Davidson motorcycles, as well as point-of-sale insurance and voluntary protection products. This segment also licenses third-party financial institutions that issue credit cards bearing the Harley-Davidson brand. Harley-Davidson, Inc. was founded in 1903 and is based in Milwaukee, Wisconsin.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Jonathan R. Root | CFO & Chief Commercial Officer | Age 51 | Compensation: $789,929 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 5K people. Revenue per employee of $813K ranks in the top quartile among Consumer Cyclical peers. Each employee generates $75K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $6K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["Harley-Davidson, Inc. is a mid-cap consumer cyclical business with a $3.3B market cap on $4.5B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -8% over the past three years and -3% annually across the full decade, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 7% against a 7% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically.","The business throws off $415M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 9 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.68\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage runs at 11.6\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 13.3% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Very elevated short interest (24.2% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Carries a 18640% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":186.39780199981982},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Consumer Cyclical tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Consumer staples outperforming discretionary, signaling cautious spending","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 76% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Piotroski score 8/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Large open-market insider purchases (net $1.2M) \u2014 management putting its own capital behind the business","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Financial quality scores above most Consumer Cyclical peers","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Harley-Davidson (NYSE:HOG) Hits New 12-Month High \u2013 Should You Buy?","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/06/harley-davidson-nysehog-hits-new-12-month-high-should-you-buy.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793970080.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.67,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"What Harley Davidson (HOG)'s Earnings Drop Means For Shareholders","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/automobiles/nyse-hog/harley-davidson/news/what-harley-davidson-hogs-earnings-drop-means-for-shareholde","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793892178.02,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.77,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Harley Davidson (HOG) Shares Climbed, What Is Behind The Fresh Attention?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/automobiles/nyse-hog/harley-davidson/news/harley-davidson-hog-shares-climbed-what-is-behind-the-fresh","date":"2026-11-02","timestamp":1793611113.827,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.922,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Can Harley-Davidson (NYSE:HOG) Keep Raising Its Guidance?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/automobile/can-harley-davidson-nysehog-keep-raising-its-guidance","date":"2026-11-02","timestamp":1793594520.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.637,"